      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. it sounds like the \"growth\" side is basically just the old-school way of looking at it, while the \"inequality\" side is the modern reality. if i were writing my paper, would it be considered more accurate to frame deregulation as a policy that prioritized short-term market expansion over long-term social stability? like, is that a fair way to characterize the fundamental trade-off?",
